THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This work contains material derived from:

    bandgap-prediction
    Copyright 2026 YZE-Crystal
    https://github.com/YZE-Crystal/bandgap-prediction
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

Files in src/ are derived from that repository. They reproduce the published
pipeline so that the audit exercises the authors' own code rather than a
re-implementation:

    src/protocol.py     70/15/15 stratified holdout split
    src/features.py     feature-column resolver
    src/gbdt.py         XGBoost training routine
    src/config.py       Optuna-tuned XGBoost hyper-parameters
    src/metrics.py      R2 / MAE / MSE scoring
    src/wrappers.py     estimator wrappers

    src/leakage.py      original to this audit (post-DFT proxy ablation)
    src/logging_util.py original to this audit

Modifications relative to upstream: the above files were extracted as a
standalone slice, import paths were rewritten to the src package, and logging
was added. No change alters the numerical behaviour of the reproduced pipeline.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATA
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Feature tables under data/ are derived from the authors' published dataset:

    Zenodo, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.18481208 (132,364 entries)

converted from the released materialsproject_data.xlsx into typed Parquet
tables. The underlying materials data originates from the Materials Project
(https://materialsproject.org), and the MEGNet identifier table derives from the
Materials Project 2018.6.1 release used by the pretrained Bandgap_MP_2018 model.

Redistribution of these derived tables is subject to the terms attached to the
original Zenodo deposit and to the Materials Project data licence.

